 "text": "Home\n/\nGovernment\n/\n Departments\n/\n Library and Community Services\n/\n Events\n/\nCommunity events\nCommunity events\nThe City of Menlo Park annually hosts citywide community events, including widely celebrated holidays, civic observances, youth initiatives, and local traditions.\nBlack Liberation Month celebration\nCelebrate 100 years of cultural significance as we reflect on the past, present, and future of Black Americans during this month of history, education, and pride.\nSpring Festival and Egg Hunt\nCelebrate spring with family, friends and neighbors in a “treasure hunt” for eggs and other surprises, a community festival and photos with the big bunny.\nCommunity Resource Fair\nJoin us for an engaging and informative resource fair for residents in the Belle Haven neighborhood and Menlo Park overall.\nYouth Poetry Voices\nElevating youth literacy and creative expression with original works of poetry created by Menlo Park youth.\nJuneteenth celebration\nJoin us to recognize Juneteenth, the oldest nationally celebrated commemoration of the ending of slavery in the United States.\n4th of July celebration\nCome dressed up in red, white and blue! Join the patriotic fun as we celebrate Independence Day with a \"people parade\" and festival.\nSummer Concert Series\nLive outdoor music with a variety of musical styles including R&B, classic rock, Latin blues, southern soul, disco and pop! Family fun for all.\nNational Night Out\nOrganize a National Night Out event on your street! Join communities and neighborhoods throughout Menlo Park and the nation.\nSummer Reading Game\nDiscover great books, experience community activities, and track your summer reading to earn prizes donated by Friends of Menlo Park Library. Open to all ages.\nHalloweek!\nCome in costume for a festive parade and fall carnival; swim in a floating pumpkin patch; go trunk-or-treating in a series of events for the whole family.\nShop local! Light Up the Season\nLight Up the Season is a festive \"winter wonderland\" themed event to ring in the holiday shopping season. Attendees are encouraged to shop and dine at local Menlo Park businesses before and after the event.\nPhotos with Santa\nThe annual Photos with Santa event takes place the second Saturday of December and provides a unique experience for your child to meet Santa and get that perfect photo opportunity.\nOther events\nThe City of Menlo Park also organizes many more smaller-scale events and programs throughout the year, such as library programs, public safety programs and other audience-specific events. These smaller-scale events build additional cultural awareness with the diverse population of Menlo Park and offer a smaller, more intimate experience compared to the larger events. \nCitywide event calendar\nEvent sponsorships\nIf you’re a local business and are interested in sponsoring an event, please read our \nSponsorship Guide\n(PDF, 2MB)\n and \npolicy\n(PDF, 163KB)\n and submit an \ninterest form\n.\nShare\nFacebook\nX\nEmail\nPrint\nLinkedIn\nBack to top",
